.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- find lines containing a search string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.B int mygrep(FILE *fp, const char *search_str, char ***matches);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mygrep
searches the file stream specified by
.I fp
for lines containing
.I search_str.
.PP
For every matching line, the function stores a dynamically allocated copy in the array pointed to by
.I matches.
The caller is responsible for freeing the allocated memory.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns the number of matching lines on success and -1 if an error occurs.
